      "html": "<ul><li>Two duties. A check by the operator at the start of each shift, which HSE's L117 says to document, as part of keeping the truck safe under PUWER 1998. A thorough examination by a competent person of the lifting parts at least every 12 months under LOLER 1998.</li><li>The pre-use check covers tyres, forks, mast, chains, hydraulics, brakes, steering, horn, lights, seatbelt and controls.</li><li>Operators need training to the standard in HSE's L117, and site familiarisation. Accreditation of training providers is voluntary.</li><li>A pad filled in later is not good proof. A timestamped record made on the spot is.</li><li>£75 per month per phone number & unlimited free dashboard accounts.</li><li>The record does not make the truck safe. An HSE inspector may ask to see it.</li></ul>"
