      "heading": "LOLER thorough examination",
      "html": "<p>The lifting parts fall under LOLER 1998. HSE's L117 lists them as the mast, chains, carriage, forks and tilt mechanism. A competent person must thoroughly examine them at least every 12 months, or in line with a written examination scheme. Trucks and attachments that lift people, and lifting accessories, need an examination at least every 6 months.</p><p>That is a formal report from a competent person, who may be from another company or a suitably trained member of your own staff. L117 says to keep the report for at least two years. Quickler does not replace it. It can store the certificate against the truck. Check the rules for your own equipment.</p>"
