      "html": "<h3>How often should a forklift be inspected in the UK?</h3><p>The operator checks it at the start of each shift, as HSE's L117 advises. A competent person thoroughly examines the lifting parts at least every 12 months (LOLER 1998), or every 6 months if the truck lifts people, or in line with a written examination scheme. Check the rule for your equipment.</p><h3>What is on a forklift pre-use check?</h3><p>Tyres, forks, backrest, mast, chains, hydraulics, brakes, steering, horn, lights, seatbelt, data plate, and warning lights. Adapt it to your trucks.</p><h3>Is a daily forklift check a legal duty?</h3><p>PUWER 1998 requires work equipment to be maintained in an efficient state and in good repair (regulation 5). HSE's L117 says the operator should check the truck at the start of each shift and document the result. L117 is guidance, so the shift check is not itself written into the Regulations. This is not legal advice.</p><h3>Can I run forklift checks in WhatsApp?</h3><p>Yes. The operator gets each item as a message. Reply with text, a voice note or a photo. A fault flags to the supervisor. No new app. No login.</p><h3>Related guides</h3><ul><li><a href=\"/pages/layered-process-audit-app-uk.html\">Layered process audit app</a></li><li><a href=\"/pages/factory-audit-software-uk.html\">Factory audit software</a></li><li><a href=\"/pages/machine-safety-inspection-checklist-uk.html\">Machine safety inspection checklist</a></li></ul>"
